# Problem Solving Process

Having a strategy for approaching problems can help students develop new insights and come up with new and better solutions. This is an iterative process that is broadly useful for solving all kinds of problems.

<img src="/blockly/media/curriculum/docs/csd/PSPE.png" alt="Cycle diagram with the steps Define, Prepare, Try, and Reflect. In the middle of the cycle is the word 'Empathize'." style="float: right; width: 30%" />

## Problem Solving Across the Curriculum

The Problem Solving Process is applied differently across different units. The following bullet points demonstrate how the process shifts throughout the AI Discoveries curriculum.
<br>

* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q10YfeMqY95SAq0VAB3wnLPK2aDuJEoD2j82n-i183Y/edit?usp=sharing" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">**The Problem Solving Process with Programming**</a> is used in mini-projects and chapter projects of Unit 3: Web Development, Unit 4b: Animations and Games, and Unit 7a/b: Creating Apps with Devices. 
<br>

* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qgiwCyO7948qPSWbTvYmR7DjH0nkh8HpfxP1HxubDis/edit?usp=sharing" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">**The Problem Solving Process with Design**</a> is primarily used in Unit 5: The Design Process. 
_This version of the Problem Solving Process does appear in the first lesson of Unit 3: Web Development, Unit 4b: Animations and Games, and Unit 7a/b: Creating Apps with Devices._
<br>

* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1e7jo729LFa6J_YoFIEDKSQHUA86_1rIILxZTdmRYQLQ/edit?usp=sharing" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">**The Problem Solving Process with Data**</a> is used in Unit 2: AI and Machine Learning and Unit 6: Data and Society.







